[2.06, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.18, "o", "\u001b[1mForeman demo\u001b[0m: no model is called; the real fm and guard hook run in a throwaway repo and Foreman home.\r\n"]
[2.68, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m1. The repo has a bug: calc.add(2, 3) returns -1. Claude tries to edit calc.py before any task exists.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.718, "o", "  \u001b[1;31mRefused\u001b[0m: Foreman: no active task in this project, so <demo>/repo/calc.py can't be edited yet. One command starts a small task: fm task new \"<title>\" --type FIX --tier S --ac \"<done when>\" --step \"<step>\" --focus (bigger work: /foreman:intake; fm next says what's next).\r\n"]
[4.918, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m2. So it plans the work first: a brief with a done-when and the command that proves it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
